Telekinesis grants the psionicist the ability to move objects through
the power of thought alone. While the most dramatic applications of
this power are seen in kinetic wave, the fundamental ability also
provides a crucial passive benefit in combat.

When an enemy successfully disarms a psionicist with telekinesis, the
power may automatically activate to catch the weapon in mid-flight.
The psionicist's mind instinctively reaches out, stopping the weapon
before it can fall and returning it instantly to their grasp.

This reactive use of telekinesis requires no conscious thought - the
trained mind simply refuses to be parted from its weapon. However,
the skill check to catch a disarmed weapon is not guaranteed. Greater
mastery of telekinesis improves the chances of successfully retrieving
the weapon before it falls.

When the power succeeds, observers see the weapon stop in mid-air and
fly back to the psionicist's hand as if by magic. When it fails, the
psionicist visibly strains for a moment but the weapon falls normally.

This passive protection against disarm attacks makes psionicists
particularly resilient combatants. Combined with their mental assault
capabilities, they can maintain both offense and defense through the
power of their minds alone.

